<title>CHINA: China corn output about 119 million T in 1996.</title>
<headline>China corn output about 119 million T in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>China produced about 119 million tonnes of corn in 1996, up from 111.986 million the year before, said an edition of the China Grains, Oils and Feeds newsletter seen in Beijing on Friday.</p>
<p>Output in the main corn growing area of Jilin province in the northeast exceeded 17.5 million tonnes last year, said the January 30 edition of the newsletter.</p>
<p>Average corn prices had fallen to 1,130 ($136) per tonne yuan at year's end from 1,463 yuan last January, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
